<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct large store sales up 0.6 pct yr/yr -- MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct large store sales up 0.6 pct yr/yr -- MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at Japanese department stores and supermarkets rose 0.6 percent in October from a year earlier to 1.89 trillion yen, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of year-on-year changes:</p>
<p>			     OCT	     SEPT (REVISED)</p>
<p>  Department stores    +1.4	     +2.0</p>
<p>  Supermarkets	   -0.1	     -1.8</p>
<p>  Total		    +0.6		 0</p>
<p>The Trade Ministry said in a statement that retail sales rose in October for the first time in four months on a year-on-year basis. Cooler weather in October contributed to brisk sales of autumn and winter clothing, the ministry said.</p>
</text>
